    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Would this work if `RequiredWidgetLifeCycle` is a union of search and recommend types, something like:\r\n\r\n```ts\r\ntype SearchWidgetLifeCycle = {\r\n  dependsOn?: 'search';\r\n  getWidgetParameters?: (state: SearchParameters, /* ... */) => SearchParameters;\r\n};\r\n\r\ntype RecommendWidgetLifeCycle = {\r\n  dependsOn: 'recommend';\r\n  getWidgetParameters?: (state: RecommendParameters, /* ... */) => RecommendParameters;\r\n};\r\n\r\ntype RequiredWidgetLifeCycle = { /* common types */ } | SearchWidgetLifeCycle | RecommendWidgetLifeCycle;\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis way contributors would not have to check for either type in their `getWidgetParameters()` implementation.",
    "commit_id": "24ee95cf13e9e05994cb654f54026ea22994ef8e",
    "created_at": "2024-03-26T09:37:36Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -216,6 +228,15 @@ type RequiredUiStateLifeCycle<TWidgetDescription extends WidgetDescription> = {\n       >;\n     }\n   ) => SearchParameters;\n+\n+  getWidgetParameters?: (\n+    state: SearchParameters | RecommendParameters,\n+    widgetSearchParametersOptions: {\n+      uiState: Expand<\n+        Partial<TWidgetDescription['indexUiState'] & IndexUiState>\n+      >;\n+    }\n+  ) => SearchParameters | RecommendParameters;",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/pull/6104#discussion_r1538885377",
